# Scope
Owned worktree `feature/work-parallel-20261103` at 8da2075 plus this change. Every
command ran with all inherited `CIEL_RUNTIME_*` variables removed. No live router,
production config, provider account or remote sandbox was started, restarted or
modified.

# Focus, discovery and parallel regression
`evidence/final-regression.txt`: 472 tests passed, 42 skipped (platform-dependent),
0 failures across 17 focused modules:

test_work_focus, test_work_discovery, test_work_discovery_pickup,
test_work_parallel, test_work_parallel_mcp, test_work_parallel_menu,
test_work_retention, test_work_mcp_tools, test_work_mod_write_gate,
test_work_breakdown_statusline, test_work_http_controller, test_work_mode_launch,
test_work_mode_packaging, test_work_mode_option, test_work_parallel_workspace,
test_external_work_discovery, test_architecture_contracts.

New/updated assertions cover: focused leaves first with unrelated leaves still
actionable and `held == 0`; a waiting focused item yielding to another runnable goal;
a blocked focused leaf not stopping other work; automatic release on completion;
selection/reorder no longer refused under focus; urgent still outranks focus and
cannot be released by focus; discovery enabled with focus set; pickup registering
while focus is set; default-on policy; P2-P5 admitted up to
`max_active - p1_reserved` with no usage observation and refused beyond; 1.0
thresholds retained only for file compatibility; menu rows reduced to 9.

# Real hook behaviour
`evidence/final-regression.txt` includes the real `register.js` scenarios (16 tests,
Node with a scripted host, no Claude Code, router or network):
- `stop-focus-unrunnable`: the focused goal's step waits, another goal has runnable
  work; Stop continues with "The next item is n5" and "call work_select with root_id
  n3", and no "stays held" text.
- `stop-discovery-focus`: nothing runnable and focus set; the discovery block is
  still emitted and no "focus only" barrier text appears.
Existing approval/discovery, restart-rebind, reviewer and concurrency scenarios
still pass.

# Deterministic root-cause reproduction
`evidence/fix-repro.py` builds Kobi's shape in a temporary board: the model focuses a
question item, its only step waits on approval, and an unrelated approved goal has a
runnable leaf. `evidence/fix-repro.json`:

- before this change (recorded at
  `docs/journal/2026/11/03/diagnostics/kobe-stall/evidence/focus-stall-repro.json`):
  actionable 0, next null, discovery disabled, reason "paused or focused";
- after: actionable 1, next "runnable research" in root n4, held 0, waiting n3,
  discovery enabled, focus auto-released after the focused step completes, and the
  next step remains the unrelated runnable one;
- parallel: file-less ledger has enabled true, max_active 3; two P2 leases were
  reserved without any usage observation and a third P2 was refused at the
  `max_active - p1_reserved` bound.

# Owned native Claude CLI E2E
`evidence/parallel-e2e-1865916e/`: real Claude Code with the packaged ciel-work mod,
the real Python dispatcher as an MCP server, and a loopback fake Anthropic gateway;
isolated HOME/config/workspace under the worktree. CLI exit 0, no hook-module
errors. `verification.json` checks: default_on true, configure true, reserve true,
bind true, child_result true, hard_cap_rejection true. `mcp.json` shows two workers
reserved and bound one at a time under `max_active=1`, with the third reservation
refused with "hard cap reached" and no usage measurement in any argument.

# Static checks
`evidence/ruff.txt`: `ruff check` passed on every changed source and test file.

# Limitations
- The E2E provider is an owned loopback fake gateway, not a production LLM round trip.
- Two child forks were dispatched in that owned E2E; the earlier worker crash/resume
  and reviewer E2E were not repeated here. Codex dispatch remains unsupported.
- Deployment is recorded in `deployment.okf`: nightly and the local snapshot are
  `fc4e6e9`. Remote sandboxes (Kobi, emily, edward) keep their installed versions
  until an explicitly approved fleet update executes.
- Automatic release is evaluated on node updates; a focus set on an already-done
  subtree is still stored until the next node update or explicit clear.
